WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.025
Today your child looks at the mark at the end of a sentence.

2
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:10.287
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:13.367
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:17.425
A period means the voice goes down, and stops. Like this.

5
00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:19.147
The cat is on the bed.

6
00:00:19.947 --> 00:00:23.085
A question mark means the voice goes up. Like this.

7
00:00:23.535 --> 00:00:24.746
Is the cat on the bed?

8
00:00:25.546 --> 00:00:29.794
You read the question, then the answer. Your child says each one after you.

9
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:34.112
Then swap. Your child asks the question, and you read the answer.

10
00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:37.645
Make it a little game. Ask it like you really want to know.

11
00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:44.305
For job two, press play on the listening track and step away. There are three questions, and three answers.

12
00:00:44.755 --> 00:00:48.688
At the end, your child asks you one question, and tells you one answer.
